  "How do marketers respond to critics who charge that promotion and packaging only add psychological, not functional, value?\nA. Marketers agree, stating that advertising and packaging add no value to products\nB. Marketers assert that lower prices are more important than branding\nC. Marketers argue that only functional products are worth the price\nD. Marketers claim that advertising and branding assure buyers of consistent quality and provide psychological benefits\nD",
